  "sections": [
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "hero",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1140,
      "heading": "Stop hand-writing AsyncAPI YAML.",
      "backgroundColor": "#0A0908",
      "callsToAction": ["15 Stars", "Get Started →"],
      "text": "15 Stars AsyncAPI 3.1.0 · AJV-validated Stop hand-writing AsyncAPI YAML. Model your event schemas, channels, and operations in TypeSpec — compile to AsyncAPI 3.1 specifications that validate against the official JSON Schema, for 22 protocols. One typed source of truth for Kafka, MQTT, AMQP, WebSocket, and 18 more — with 30 decorators, spec-generated protocol bindings, and a 270+-test compliance suite. Get Started → pnpm add @lars-artmann/typespec-asyncapi api.tsp import \"@lars-artmann/typespec-asyncapi\"; using TypeSpec.AsyncAPI; namespace MyAPI; model Event { id: string; timestamp: utcDateTime",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1140,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 602,
      "heading": "From TypeSpec to AsyncAPI in 30 seconds",
      "backgroundColor": "#110E0C",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "SEE IT WORK From TypeSpec to AsyncAPI in 30 seconds One compile: a typed TypeSpec definition becomes a validated AsyncAPI 3.1 document with channels, operations, messages, and schemas. demo.mp4 — 30s product tour See it work end-to-end — 30 seconds, no audio required.",
      "layout": "split",
      "assetUrls": ["http://localhost:4321/demo.mp4"]
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1742,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 903,
      "heading": "Typed in. Validated out.",
      "backgroundColor": "#0A0908",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "WHY THIS EMITTER Typed in. Validated out. Everything between your TypeSpec source and a spec-compliant AsyncAPI 3.1 document is table-driven, tested, and deterministic. Validated AsyncAPI 3.1 Every byte of output is checked against the official AsyncAPI 3.1.0 JSON Schema (AJV) across a 270+-test compliance suite — invalid specs cannot ship. 22 protocols, 19 bindings Kafka, MQTT, AMQP, WebSocket, NATS, and more. All bindings auto-generated from @asyncapi/specs with version auto-injection and placement checking. 30 typed decorators Channels, messages, servers, security schemes, traits, parameter",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2644,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 698,
      "heading": "Model, compile, validate, ship",
      "backgroundColor": "#110E0C",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "HOW IT WORKS Model, compile, validate, ship Four deterministic steps from typed source to a spec-compliant AsyncAPI document. 01 Model in TypeSpec Define event schemas, channels, operations, servers, and security in one typed language. Decorators carry AsyncAPI semantics; the compiler carries the validation. 02 Compile with tsp tsp compile resolves imports, checks 30 diagnostics, and hands the type graph to the emitter — invalid protocols and misplaced bindings never reach the output. 03 Emit the spec A table-driven schema pipeline maps every scalar, constraint, union, and generic instantiatio",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3342,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 838,
      "heading": "This emitter vs the alternatives",
      "backgroundColor": "#0A0908",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "COMPARISON This emitter vs the alternatives Measured against the other TypeSpec AsyncAPI emitter and the hand-written YAML status quo (August 2026). Capability typespec-asyncapi tsp-asyncapi Hand-written YAML AsyncAPI version 3.1.0 (latest) 3.0.0 any Output validation 270+ AJV compliance tests 15 property tests Spectral, at best Protocols 22, bindings spec-generated 13, hand-written manual per protocol Reusable components 7 slots, 11 decorators not supported copy-paste Multi-file output split-schemas + $ref rewrite not supported manual Compile-time diagnostics 30 codes deferred lint only Typed",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4180,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 825,
      "heading": "Built for event-driven teams",
      "backgroundColor": "#110E0C",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "USE CASES Built for event-driven teams Where a typed, validated AsyncAPI source of truth pays for itself. AsyncAPI as code Schemas, examples, security schemes, and bindings regenerate from source — the spec can no longer drift from the system it describes. Multi-protocol estates One TypeSpec namespace, Kafka + MQTT + WebSocket bindings with auto-injected versions and spec-checked placements across 22 protocols. CI compliance gates Every build emits documents that pass the official AsyncAPI 3.1.0 JSON Schema — contract violations fail the pipeline, not production. Docs that stay current Descrip",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5004,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 479,
      "heading": "Your first validated spec is one compile away",
      "backgroundColor": "#0A0908",
      "callsToAction": ["Read the Quick Start →", "View on GitHub"],
      "text": "GET STARTED Your first validated spec is one compile away Install the emitter, add two decorators to a TypeSpec file, and generate AsyncAPI 3.1 that already passes the official JSON Schema. Read the Quick Start → View on GitHub",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    }
